READY TO DEPLOY (merged into development, not on the server yet; dev1 deploys)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- CloudDev, PR #937 (#437 part 3, #919; skip if core on the server already includes commit
  32e7bd4): core only, no migration or setting. Nothing visible while DMBOT_ENFORCE_PLANS is
  off (it stays off until go-live, #498), so the check is only that core starts with no ERROR
  and that these still work as before: 🤖 Find names on a pasted list, `/dmbot backup` and
  `/dmbot restore`, and a transcript download button. With the setting on (go-live only): a
  Try It owner is refused a copy and a transcript in plain words, a player is told to ask the
  owner, and an ended plan is told "Your plan has ended, so DMbot can't <do that>".

- dev2, PR #942 (#931): core with **migration 0035_rules_cards** (a new column
  `campaigns.rules_cards`, off by default; the migration runs when core starts, so rebuild
  core; keep the migration list sorted with #944's 0036 if that lands too). No setting. Rules
  cards from the table: when a spell, condition or creature is named at a live table, a short
  card goes on the DM screen, if the DM turned it on. A 5-minute live check with the setting
  on, as a DM: press **Settings** on the DM screen, then **Turn rules cards on** (the card's
  line says "Rules cards: On"); start listening; say "I cast Fireball": a card on the DM
  screen with "Heard: …", the source and "You decide", and nothing in the transcript channel;
  wait a minute; say "the goblin is grappled": the **Goblin Warrior** card appears and takes
  that minute (the first name not yet shown wins), so a minute later say "it is grappled" for
  the Grappled card; say "a light in the dark" or "what a nightmare": nothing. Press **Got it**
  (buttons go), **Read it all** (the full rule, privately), **Ignore** on another card (it says
  how to stop all cards) and **Override** (the Add a house rule form with Fireball already in
  "Instead of"). A player pressing a button is refused. Turn it off again with **Turn rules
  cards off**. Core logs no ERROR.

